{"id": "school-bond-committee-empty-audits-late", "title": "School bonds: watchdog committee left empty, audits took up to 30 months", "seconds": 137.1, "voice": "elevenlabs:OUMCzFUTd0F4Q6lkLkco", "narrator": "Roxy", "tempo": 1.2, "made": "2026-11-25", "key": "12a4eb2c9b0cd144", "words": 443, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["amount", "suspicious[0]", "established[2]"], "text": "223.4 million dollars of school bond money, spent in just two school years.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 4.62, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$223.4 million", "label": "school bond money spent while the oversight committee had no members", "sub": "2018-19 and 2019-20"}, "emph": ["223.4 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.42, 0.89, 1.14, 1.39, 1.69, 2.02, 2.1, 2.4, 2.66, 2.91, 3.19, 3.27, 3.49, 3.69, 4.0]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]", "established[1]"], "text": "By the State’s rules, a citizens’ committee of at least seven members reviews that spending.", "t0": 5.04, "t1": 9.17, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "Citizens’ Bond Oversight Committee", "kicker": "The State’s bond rules", "sub": "at least seven members"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.23, 0.56, 0.96, 1.05, 1.56, 1.93, 2.01, 2.09, 2.28, 2.59, 2.98, 3.38, 3.58]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "In those two years, the district’s own auditor reported, the committee had no members at all.", "t0": 9.29, "t1": 13.28, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "Citizens’ Bond Oversight Committee", "kicker": "The State’s bond rules", "sub": "at least seven members"}, "emph": ["no members"], "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.36, 0.56, 0.84, 0.94, 1.39, 1.63, 2.03, 2.43, 2.52, 2.87, 3.04, 3.22, 3.57, 3.66]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[0]", "pa19"], "text": "The 2019 audit said every member had reached their term limit, and none was replaced.", "t0": 13.5, "t1": 18.06, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "The District’s CBOC members reached their term‐limits at the beginning of the 2018‐19 fiscal year and have not been replaced.", "kicker": "Bond performance audit, 2019, Conclusion I"}, "emph": ["none was replaced"], "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.38, 0.77, 1.08, 1.29, 1.55, 1.81, 1.94, 2.19, 2.38, 2.66, 3.32, 3.57, 3.79, 3.96]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "timeline[1]"], "text": "Its 2020 audit repeats the finding, but dates the start a year later.", "t0": 18.18, "t1": 21.82, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["2019 audit", "from mid-2018"], "b": ["2020 audit", "from mid-2019"], "kicker": "When the committee emptied", "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.48, 0.77, 1.06, 1.44, 1.54, 2.04, 2.22, 2.5, 2.6, 2.93, 3.02, 3.25]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "span", "ref": ["established[0]", "timeline[4]"], "text": "New members were appointed only in April and May 2021.", "t0": 21.94, "t1": 25.32, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "span", "from": "2018-07-01", "to": "2021-05", "days": null, "fromLab": "term limits reached", "toLab": "new members appointed", "kicker": "No members"}, "emph": ["April and May 2021"], "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.56, 0.68, 1.12, 1.4, 1.54, 1.95, 2.11, 2.43, 2.77]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[2]", "suspicious[0].what", "suspicious[0].why"], "text": "Meanwhile the bonds kept spending, and far more in the second year.", "t0": 25.44, "t1": 28.67, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["2018-19", "$64,202,313"], "b": ["2019-20", "$159,237,859"], "kicker": "Bond spending, three measures together", "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.45, 0.55, 0.91, 1.15, 1.68, 1.9, 2.18, 2.4, 2.48, 2.58, 2.88]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[5]", "fs22"], "text": "Once it was back, bond books were adjusted for 2018 and 2020 costs, at its chair’s request.", "t0": 28.79, "t1": 34.33, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "fs22", "kicker": "2016 Measure A bond fund audit, 2022", "text": "Bond funded staff benefit costs adjustment to FY2018 and FY2020 cost per CBOC Chair request", "mark": "per CBOC Chair"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.33, 0.46, 0.8, 1.1, 1.36, 1.48, 1.92, 2.05, 2.42, 2.95, 3.11, 3.44, 3.79, 4.28, 4.45, 4.62, 4.95]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]"], "text": "With no committee, the yearly audits were the check left. How late did they come out?", "t0": 34.55, "t1": 38.75, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "The yearly bond audits", "kicker": "Report dates", "sub": "months after the year ended"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.35, 0.75, 0.85, 1.17, 1.5, 1.62, 1.7, 1.99, 2.89, 3.15, 3.35, 3.47, 3.59, 3.78]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[3]", "timeline[5]"], "text": "Up to 30 months after the year ended.", "t0": 38.75, "t1": 40.54, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "30 months", "label": "after the year ended: the 2020 bond audit", "sub": "dated 13 January 2023"}, "emph": ["30 months"], "wt": [0.04, 0.2, 0.3, 0.6, 0.9, 1.14, 1.24, 1.46]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[3]", "ba"], "text": "The 2017 audit came out in about 8 months. The 2019 audit took 21.", "t0": 41.06, "t1": 45.45, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["2016-17 audit", "8 months"], "b": ["2018-19 audit", "21 months"], "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.39, 0.84, 1.13, 1.32, 1.48, 1.54, 1.79, 2.01, 2.53, 2.68, 2.95, 3.33, 3.6, 3.78]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "gl20"], "text": "The one reason the auditor gave for 2020: it waited for the committee’s own report.", "t0": 45.57, "t1": 50.03, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "The issuance of our report was delayed for the Citizen’s Bond Oversight Committee to formalize its parallel report", "kicker": "Auditor’s letter to the Board of Education, 13 January 2023"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.36, 0.67, 0.77, 1.15, 1.36, 1.5, 1.8, 2.6, 2.78, 3.05, 3.16, 3.24, 3.66, 3.92]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[3]", "timeline[7]"], "text": "By 2024-25 the delay was back down to 8 months, with no findings.", "t0": 50.15, "t1": 54.52, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "calendar", "label": "8 months", "kicker": "2024-25 bond audits", "sub": "no findings"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.44, 0.93, 1.0, 1.68, 1.79, 2.07, 2.21, 2.45, 2.67, 2.76, 3.0, 3.36, 3.58, 3.75]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "fs20"], "text": "Then the 2020 audit’s material weakness. What cash did the 2016 bond’s books show?", "t0": 54.74, "t1": 60.67, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "2016 bond fund", "kicker": "Finding 2020-001, material weakness", "sub": "cash before the auditor’s adjustments"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.24, 0.57, 0.91, 1.27, 1.71, 2.81, 3.08, 3.47, 3.62, 3.69, 4.02, 4.51, 4.85, 5.13]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[4]"], "text": "Minus 39.7 million dollars.", "t0": 60.67, "t1": 62.94, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "minus $39.7 million", "label": "cash in the 2016 bond fund’s books", "sub": "year ended 30 June 2020"}, "emph": ["Minus 39.7 million"], "wt": [0.04, 0.42, 0.88, 1.14, 1.43, 1.76]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "established[4]"], "text": "Why below zero? It had borrowed 39.8 million from the 2011 bond, until a bond sale.", "t0": 63.36, "t1": 69.44, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "money", "name": "2011 bond fund", "sub": "lent $39,793,013"}, {"art": "money", "name": "2016 bond fund", "sub": "until the August 2020 bond sale"}], "kicker": "Temporary cash flow support"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.29, 0.58, 1.7, 1.87, 1.99, 2.32, 2.85, 3.12, 3.34, 3.69, 3.85, 3.92, 4.21, 4.52, 4.98, 5.27, 5.33, 5.66]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "When was it repaid? The notes say August 2020; the district’s response, August 2021.", "t0": 69.56, "t1": 75.73, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["the notes", "repaid August 2020"], "b": ["the district’s response", "repaid August 2021"], "kicker": "Two repayment dates", "arrows": false}, "emph": ["August 2021"], "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.35, 0.46, 1.61, 1.78, 2.04, 2.37, 2.69, 2.96, 3.77, 3.91, 4.3, 4.93, 5.27, 5.55]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[2].why"], "text": "Both dates cannot be right.", "t0": 75.85, "t1": 77.2, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["the notes", "repaid August 2020"], "b": ["the district’s response", "repaid August 2021"], "kicker": "Two repayment dates", "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.36, 0.64, 0.94, 1.07]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[6]", "timeline[6]"], "text": "In 2023-24, 33.8 million dollars of costs moved from the 2011 bond to the 2016 bond.", "t0": 77.42, "t1": 84.35, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "money", "name": "2011 bond fund", "sub": "$33,816,663"}, {"art": "money", "name": "2006 bond fund", "sub": "$1,110,868"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "2016 bond fund", "sub": "to shift qualified construction costs"}], "kicker": "2023-24"}, "emph": ["33.8 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.45, 0.95, 1.03, 1.73, 2.25, 2.5, 2.72, 3.04, 3.37, 3.47, 3.89, 4.11, 4.24, 4.32, 4.58, 4.9, 5.53, 5.71, 5.79, 6.07, 6.54]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[6]", "fs23"], "text": "A year earlier, the 2016 bond was repaid for student devices it had fronted.", "t0": 84.47, "t1": 88.68, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "$7,700,044", "kicker": "2022-23: repaid to the 2016 fund", "sub": "student devices it had fronted"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.44, 0.83, 0.9, 1.19, 1.68, 1.96, 2.11, 2.56, 2.7, 3.05, 3.52, 3.63, 3.75]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "established[7]"], "text": "And the 2016 plan was redrawn: security now has four times its board-approved share.", "t0": 88.8, "t1": 93.99, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["security, board-approved", "$10,000,000"], "b": ["security, June 2026", "$40,352,285"], "kicker": "The 2016 bond’s plan", "arrows": false}, "emph": ["four times"], "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.21, 0.47, 0.92, 1.25, 1.42, 2.4, 2.93, 3.12, 3.34, 3.6, 3.96, 4.14, 4.77]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "suspicious[3].why", "established[7]"], "text": "Schoolyards have more than three times theirs; modernization has 84.2 million dollars less.", "t0": 94.11, "t1": 99.9, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["schoolyards, board-approved", "$14,000,000"], "b": ["schoolyards, June 2026", "$48,629,170"], "kicker": "Modernization: $84.2 million less", "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.68, 0.83, 0.99, 1.15, 1.4, 1.73, 2.74, 3.52, 3.72, 4.22, 4.46, 4.68, 5.0, 5.36]}, {"scene": "record", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[9]"], "text": "The district said its general audit was late because it switched auditors.", "t0": 100.12, "t1": 103.35, "shot": "record-9-6 May 2024", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "fb10", "text": "6 May 2024", "mark": "6 May 2024", "kicker": "San Francisco Unified School District"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.5, 0.67, 0.83, 1.17, 1.43, 1.58, 1.88, 2.14, 2.24, 2.65]}, {"scene": "record", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[10]"], "text": "George Washington High School finished above bid. The table leaves the cause open.", "t0": 103.47, "t1": 107.82, "shot": "doc10", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "changes16", "kicker": "Board of Education", "text": "25.37% above bid", "mark": "25.37% above bid"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.32, 0.81, 1.01, 1.31, 1.65, 1.93, 2.63, 2.79, 3.16, 3.44, 3.54, 3.89]}, {"scene": "record", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[11]"], "text": "In June 2021 the committee met and planned to review three years of audits.", "t0": 107.94, "t1": 111.91, "shot": "doc11", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "minutes21", "kicker": "Board of Education", "text": "7 June 2021", "mark": "7 June 2021"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.48, 0.77, 1.33, 1.43, 1.75, 2.01, 2.13, 2.41, 2.51, 2.83, 3.08, 3.34, 3.44]}, {"scene": "record", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[12]"], "text": "A resolution in the committee packet lists six uses for money from the proposed arts center.", "t0": 112.03, "t1": 116.19, "shot": "doc12", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "allocation16", "kicker": "Board of Education", "text": "$100 million", "mark": "$100 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.67, 0.75, 0.83, 1.14, 1.52, 1.74, 2.04, 2.37, 2.54, 2.78, 2.94, 3.01, 3.45, 3.72]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[8]", "notEstablished[0]"], "text": "Every year, the auditors found bond money went only to projects the voters listed.", "t0": 116.41, "t1": 120.32, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Only listed projects", "kicker": "Performance audits, 2022-23 to 2024-25", "sub": "no findings"}, "emph": ["only"], "wt": [0.0, 0.33, 0.59, 0.71, 1.17, 1.43, 1.71, 1.96, 2.15, 2.38, 2.48, 2.99, 3.1, 3.46]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[1]", "notEstablished[2]", "notEstablished[3]"], "text": "Not known: why the committee sat empty so long, and what the board approved first.", "t0": 120.44, "t1": 124.92, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["Which start date of the vacancy is right", "When the $39.8 million loan was repaid", "What the board approved before costs moved between bonds"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.31, 1.19, 1.46, 1.55, 1.87, 2.12, 2.43, 2.64, 3.0, 3.15, 3.3, 3.38, 3.61, 4.0]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[1]", "next[2]"], "text": "What would settle it? The committee’s minutes, the loan ledger, and the board’s approvals.", "t0": 125.04, "t1": 129.61, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "Board of Education", "what": "The committee’s minutes and annual reports, 2018-2021"}, {"who": "District business office", "what": "The ledger of the 2011-to-2016 loan"}, {"who": "Board of Education", "what": "The approvals behind the $33.8 million shift"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.29, 0.59, 1.29, 1.45, 1.84, 2.42, 2.6, 2.86, 3.28, 3.46, 3.54, 3.85]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status"], "text": "These are the district’s own auditors’ statements; none is a finding of misuse.", "t0": 129.73, "t1": 133.89, "shot": "b24", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.33, 0.4, 0.84, 1.09, 1.52, 2.61, 2.88, 3.01, 3.07, 3.47, 3.57]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "Every source is linked in the case file below.", "t0": 134.01, "t1": 136.2, "shot": "b25", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.34, 0.67, 0.81, 1.08, 1.15, 1.23, 1.48, 1.75]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "Two years, no watchdog", "lead1": "Empty chairs", "lead2": "Late audits", "lead3": "Below zero", "lead4": "Between measures", "close": "Where it stands", "record": "The public record"}, "look": "terminal", "hook": "number"}